\subsection{Excluding known interpretations}

\textbf{Not a quantum phase transition.} The ground-state energy gap remains non-zero throughout the scan interval.

\textbf{Not an entanglement entropy singularity.} The enhanced diagnosis uses the standard deviation of the entanglement spectrum, which is sensitive to the spectral tail, not the Shannon entropy, which is dominated by the bulk.

\textbf{Not a scar-state crossing.} The chemical potential defect modulates the entire relational field, not just the scar subspace.

\textbf{Finite-size trend.} At $L=14$, no signal; at $L=16$, weak; at $L=18$, clear. The signal strengthens with system size, indicating emergent behavior.

\subsection{Tail-slope verification}

The tail slope of the entanglement spectrum changed by $0.0313$ at $\mu\approx1.5$, exceeding the maximum background change of $0.0290$. This confirms a global reorganization through the entire spectrum.

\subsection{TAT blind test}

Marat Sultanov's TAT-Defense blind test detected only boundary anchors ($\mu=0.0$, $\mu=2.0$) and was silent at $\mu\approx1.5$, correctly recognizing the jump as a smooth modulation, not a sharp transition.

\section{Independent replication in a self-built fractal system}

\subsection{Setup}

We generate a system from a Sierpi\'{n}ski fractal graph (level 2): $N=15$ nodes, $27$ edges, $32768$-dimensional Hilbert space. A contradiction edge $(0,2)$ is implanted, connecting vertices of two different sub-triangles. The strength $s$ is scanned from $0$ to $3.0$.

\subsection{Results}

The data are shown in Fig.~\ref{fig:fractal} and Table~\ref{tab:fractal}. The enhanced diagnosis falls by an absolute amount of $0.125$ ($60\%$ of its initial value) from $0.2093$ at $s=0$ to $0.0843$ at $s=0.50$, then rises monotonically to $0.2878$. The default diagnosis shows irregular fluctuations in the range $[0.02, 0.07]$ but no valley matching the enhanced diagnosis. This is the defining signature of Silent Discordance: the relational observable re-organizes sharply, while the entity observable only jitters aimlessly.

